{
 "uid": "utm-obs-08-coverage",
 "title": "08 - Observability Coverage",
 "description": "**Purpose:** state honestly which parts of the UTM platform are observable and which are not. This dashboard exists so that a silent gap is never mistaken for a healthy signal.\n\n**Data sources:** Prometheus (self-inspection: targets, ServiceMonitors, blackbox probes, kube-state-metrics inventory).\n\n**Design rule:** no panel on this dashboard renders an empty chart to represent a missing capability. Gaps are declared as text with the evidence that proves them, because an empty time series reads as *nothing is wrong* rather than *nothing is being measured*.\n\n**Current headline gaps:** UTM application services expose no Prometheus metrics (no RED); application logs do not exist; synthetic probe coverage is ~9% of ingresses; Jaeger traces stop at 2026-04-14.",
 "tags": [
  "utm-observability",
  "coverage",
  "gaps"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
