  {
   "id": 120,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Distributed Tracing — STALE",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 20,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 39
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "code": {
     "language": "plaintext",
     "showLineNumbers": false,
     "showMiniMap": false
    },
    "content": "# Status: **STALE DATA**\n\nJaeger is connected to Grafana and holds roughly **5,145 spans**, but the backing indices are:\n\n```\njaeger-jaeger-span-2026-03-19    1292\njaeger-jaeger-span-2026-03-23     383\njaeger-jaeger-span-2026-04-08     100\njaeger-jaeger-span-2026-04-14    3360\n```\n\nThe most recent span index is **2026-04-14**. Jaeger is **not** live application tracing and must not be read as such.\n\n### Additional limitation\n\nThe Jaeger datasource is configured with `tracesToLogsV2` pointing at `es-logs-uid` — the log datasource whose index does not exist. Trace→log navigation is therefore non-functional.\n\n### Navigation\n\nTracing remains available for historical investigation via **Explore → Jaeger** and **Explore → Tempo**. It is intentionally not embedded as a live panel in this suite, because doing so would imply current trace coverage that does not exist."
   },
   "pluginVersion": "12.1.1",
   "transparent": false
  },
  {
   "id": 121,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Coverage Summary & Alerting Data",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 20,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 12,
    "y": 39
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "code": {
     "language": "plaintext",
     "showLineNumbers": false,
     "showMiniMap": false
    },
    "content": "# Observability coverage at a glance\n\nRe-measured 2026-10-02.\n\n| Layer | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kubernetes infrastructure | ✅ **COVERED** | kube-state-metrics, 69 utm pods visible |\n| Node resources | ✅ **COVERED** | node-exporter on all 4 nodes |\n| Ceph / storage | ✅ **COVERED** | ceph-mgr scraped (ServiceMonitor added by this work) |\n| PVC utilisation | ✅ **COVERED** | kubelet volume stats |\n| Ingress edge (rate / status / latency) | ✅ **COVERED** | `nginx_ingress_controller_*`, 52 request series, 624 histogram buckets (ServiceMonitor added by this work) |\n| Identity provider runtime | ✅ **COVERED** | Keycloak JVM, GC, threads, Agroal DB pool, Vert.x worker pool — 159 series (ServiceMonitor added by this work) |\n| Application logs | ✅ **COVERED** | Loki + `alloy-logs` DaemonSet (added by this work); health check OK, real log data verified flowing from multiple namespaces across all 4 nodes |\n| Business data (ES) | ⚠️ **HISTORICAL** | datasets end Aug 2026 at the latest |\n| Endpoint uptime | ⚠️ **PARTIAL** | 3 of 32 ingresses probed |\n| Distributed tracing | ⚠️ **STALE** | newest span index 2026-04-14 |\n| Keycloak login / token counters | ❌ **NOT INSTRUMENTED** | needs the `keycloak-metrics-spi` extension, not bundled in this image |\n| Application RED metrics | ❌ **NOT INSTRUMENTED** | 0 `http_*`/`grpc_*` series from utm-*; no UTM service exposes `/metrics` |\n| App-level structured logs (ES) | ❌ **NOT AVAILABLE** | `utm-services-logs*` index still does not exist — separate from container logs above, not yet proposed |\n\nScrape footprint: **16** distinct jobs, **53** targets. Panel *Targets Down* above is live — treat any non-zero value as current, not as a figure quoted here.\n\n---\n\n### Alert history\n\n`utm-alerting-statistics` contains **0 documents** across all four of its indices. No alert-history panel is built from it — charting an empty index would render a flat line that looks like *no alerts fired*, when the truth is *nothing was ever recorded*.\n\nAlerting state should come from **Grafana Alerting / Prometheus** instead. Rules are supplied with this suite in `alert-rules.yaml`.\n"
   },
   "pluginVersion": "12.1.1",
   "transparent": false
  }
